# Everything an agent working on Laika needs to know about its environment.
#
# Copy to `.env.agent` at the repo root (gitignored by `.env*`) and fill in the
# blanks you have been given. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC: never commit a filled
# copy, and never paste a secret into a doc, a task file, a log or a commit.
#
# Named `agent.env.example`, not `.env.example`, for the reason
# docker/env.example gives: the repo ignores `.env*`, so a dot-prefixed example
# would never be seen. See docs/HANDOVER.md §5 for how each credential is
# obtained.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the repository
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=PawanSirsat/Laika
GITHUB_DEFAULT_BRANCH=master           # a push here is a production release (D-073)
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Pawan Sirsat"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=48860105+PawanSirsat@users.noreply.github.com
# Your own access, created for you by the owner — never the owner's token.
# A fine-grained token for this repository only: Contents read/write,
# Actions read/write. Leave empty if you push through an authenticated `gh`.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- production
# The production address — an Elastic IP, HTTP only until a domain is added.
# Deliberately not written in this public repo (LAI-627). Read it from the
# `laika` stack's `Url` output, or take it from the owner:
#   aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name laika --query "Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='Url'].OutputValue" --output text
LAIKA_URL=
# A Laika personal access token for YOUR agent identity: Settings → Tokens on
# the board, format lai_<40 chars>, shown once. Used by the MCP endpoint at
# ${LAIKA_URL}/mcp and by the plugin's hooks.
LAIKA_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- AWS (not needed for development)
AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=926583575159
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_PROFILE=laika                      # the owner's local profile name; yours may differ
LAIKA_INSTANCE_ID=i-0b2fa45c15e1b10cf
LAIKA_ECR_REPOSITORY=926583575159.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/laika
LAIKA_STACK_SERVER=laika               # docker/aws/laika-ec2.yaml
LAIKA_STACK_DEPLOY_ROLE=laika-github-deploy   # infra/github-deploy-role.yml
LAIKA_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::926583575159:role/laika-github-deploy
# Access for an agent is the owner's to grant: an IAM Identity Center user or a
# role limited to SSM on the instance and read access to ECR and CloudFormation.
# Configure it as an AWS profile; do not put access keys here unless the owner
# gives you keys and asks for exactly that.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets that stay where they are
# LAIKA_SECRET (production) lives in AWS Secrets Manager as LaikaSecret-sJ4X5Zj0paxP-…,
# generated inside AWS and read only by the instance at boot into
# /opt/laika/.env. You never need it. Do not copy it out.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local development
# The server refuses to start without a secret of 32+ characters. Generate a
# throwaway one for your machine; never reuse production's.
#   export LAIKA_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 48)"
LAIKA_SECRET=
PORT=3000                              # the API; Vite serves the web app on 5173
# LAIKA_DB_PATH=./data/laika.db        # the default outside production
